23 | fields | In July 1863 the McClean farm was farmed by a tenant | - | 1863-07 | stated | The report says it is hard to determine whether the McCleans ever farmed the farm themselves or always leased it out to tenants, as was the case in July 1863 | =It is hard to determine how long the McCleans had owned the farm and whether they had ever farmed it themselves or had always leased it out to {{tennants|tenants}}, as was the case in July 1863.
23 | general | Moses McClean bought two tracts of 71 acres on the Mummasburg Road on April 3, 1854 | - | 1854 (purchase) | stated | The report says Moses McClean purchased two tracts of land, a total of 71 acres, on the Mummasburg Road on April 3, 1854 | =Moses McClean had bought and sold considerable amounts of real estate during the 1840's and 1850's including the purchase of two tracts of land, a total {{36|}} of 71 acres, on the Mummasburg Road on April 3, 1854.
25 | buildings | The report says the barn and house look much as they did 105 years before 1968 | STR-MCLEAN-HOUSE1,STR-MCLEAN-BARN1 | ~1968 compared with July 1863 (hedged: much as) | hedged | The report says that in 1968 the barn and house look much as they did 105 years earlier, on the afternoon of July 1, 1863 | At present the barn and house look much as they did 105 years ago when on the afternoon of July 1 the soldiers of the North and South contested for victory on the fields north of Gettysburg, Pennsylvania.
