26 | fences | Confederate artillery camped on the farm on the night of June 26, 1863 and destroyed a large amount of fencing, hay and ham | - | 1863-06-26 | stated | The report transcribes the claim, which says that on the night of June 26, 1863 about two regiments of Rebel artillery encamped on the farm and destroyed a large amount of fencing, hay and ham | =On the night of 26 June 1863 about two regiments of Rebel Artillery encamped upon his farm destroyed a large amount of fencing, hay, and ham.
26 | fields | New York cavalry camped on one of McClean's clover fields on June 30 | - | 1863-06-30 | stated | The report transcribes the claim, which says that on June 30 a large force of New York Cavalry encamped upon one of his clover fields, extended over most of the place | =On the 30th of June a large force of New York Cavalry encamped upon one of his clover fields extended over most of the place.
27 | fences | Coleman found the fences destroyed and the growing crops greatly injured on July 5 | - | 1863-07-05 (sworn statement of Nov. 11, 1868) | stated | The report transcribes the sworn statement of Robert C. Coleman, who on the 5th visited the McClean farm and found the fences destroyed, the growing crops greatly injured and the buildings injured by the Rebels during their occupancy | On the 5th deponent visited the farm of claimant found the fences destroyed and growing crops greatly injured and buildings injured by the Rebels during their occupancy.
